        "en": "A complementary specialty programme, or fellowship, is a shorter and highly focused period of training that equips a specialist or subspecialist with practical skills in a narrow clinical area or a specific technique. These programmes are defined under the parent disciplines listed below, each of which offers one or more approved fellowships."
